@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed — Artifact usability, lifecycle and presence dimensions
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

state "Usability" as U {
 [*] --> Uploading
 Uploading --> Available : actual validation / usable evidence
 Uploading --> Unavailable : interrupted / rejected / uncertain
 Available --> Unavailable : integrity / presence no longer established
}
state "Logical lifecycle (source-defined)" as L {
 state Active
 state "Retired / archived candidate" as Archived
 state "Trash / deletion requested candidate" as Trash
 Active --> Archived : reviewed owner policy
 Active --> Trash : reviewed explicit lifecycle command
 Trash --> Active : permitted restore and current usable checks
}
note bottom of L
 Locked is a coordination claim, not necessarily lifecycle.
 Trash is not physical deletion; archived is not cold storage.
 Protected references can block reclamation in any lifecycle state.
end note

@enduml
